## Purpose of Read Later

**Read Later** is your personal reading queue: articles, videos, podcasts, and documents you intend to finish—not just skim. Unlike feeds (publisher-driven), Read Later is **you-driven**. You choose what enters the queue and when it leaves.

Press `⌘2` on macOS to jump to Read Later, or `⌘⌥L` to switch the sidebar into Read Later mode.

## How items enter the queue

Common capture paths:

- **Save to Read Later** — actions palette (`⌘⇧A`) or share extension
- **From feeds** — save while triaging without marking the feed item “done” for your purposes
- **Quick Add** (`⌘N`) — when configured to target Read Later
- **Import** — documents and imports may land here by type

**Remove from Read Later** (palette) returns an item to a non-queue state without deleting the card.

## Collections and filters

The sidebar exposes curated **collections**—filtered views over the same queue:

| Collection | Typical use |
|------------|-------------|
| **In Progress** | Partially read long pieces |
| **Read** | Completed queue items |
| **Archived** | Cleared from active queue, retained |
| **Highlights** | Items with reader highlights |
| **Books** | EPUB and long-form book-like items |
| **PDFs** | PDF documents in the queue |
| **Markdown** | Markdown files |
| **Statistics** | Reading stats for queue activity |

Open any collection from the sidebar or **Command palette** (`⌘K`) → “Go to In Progress”, “Go to PDFs”, etc.

{% note %}
Collection names in the palette match `AppCommandCatalog` Go To entries. They do not have separate keyboard shortcuts beyond `⌘2` for the mode itself.
{% /note %}

## Starred Read Later

`⌘4` jumps to **Starred Read Later**—important items within the queue. This differs from:

- Starred **feed articles** (Feeds mode, starred articles collection)
- Starred **bookmarks** (Bookmarks mode)

Use stars (`⌘⇧S`) to float priority items within whichever list you are viewing.

## Read states and habits

Healthy queue habits:

1. **Capture freely** — Share extension and Quick Add lower friction
2. **Triage weekly** — Triage layout + In Progress to resume or archive
3. **Mark read deliberately** — `⌘E` when done, not when merely opening
4. **Archive instead of hoarding** — palette Archive clears active lists without delete

**Mark all as read** (`⌘⇧R`) applies to the current list context—use carefully on Unread-style views.

## Move and organize

**Move…** (`⌘⇧M`) transfers items between Bookmarks folders, Read Later collections, or related destinations depending on context. The catalog title is **Move…**, not “Move to folder”.

Combine **Manage Tags…** (`⌘⇧T`) with **smart lists** for cross-cutting views (e.g. all tagged `research` across Read Later).

## Media in the queue

YouTube and podcast cards can play in the reader. PDFs and EPUBs open with document-appropriate chrome. See [Reading Tools](/docs/reading-tools) and [Documents](/docs/documents).

## Sync

Read Later metadata—read position, stars, tags, archive state—syncs via iCloud. Large file bytes for imports may remain device-local; see Documents guide.

